      "content": "thanks. it's a decent start but a bit vague. it feels a little too \"polite\" or surface-level. \n\nthe reviewer wants to see much more biting, technical scrutiny. the score for rigor usually spikes when the reviewer identifies specific \"flaws\" or \"limitations\" in the actual logic. \n\ncan you make it much more intense? go deeper into the actual methodology—like questioning the memory compression or the sliding window—and don't be afraid to be more critical. just, again, try to stay focused on the actual tech so it doesn't look like you're just throwing out negative words for no reason.",
